  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Architecture**\n\nI\'m solidifying the core architecture. It\'s clear this \"College Hub Launcher\" demands a Next.js (App Router, TypeScript) foundation, enhanced with Supabase for data management. It\'s a single-sign-on entry point, featuring a dashboard with four links: Clubspace, Canteen, AI Content Detector, and Skiptray, all opening in new tabs. I see its value as a central login and navigation point.\n\n\n**Resolving Conflicting Instructions**\n\nI\'m wrestling with conflicting instructions and environment constraints. The AI Studio expects a Vite/React SPA, yet the user explicitly requested a Next.js 14+ App Router project. While the environment leans towards Vite, I\'m exploring the feasibility of integrating Next.js within this setup. I\'m checking dependencies and investigating how to make Next.js work on port 3000, which is the system default.\n\n\n**Adapting to Platform Constraints**\n\nI\'m now focusing on reconciling the user\'s Next.js request with the Vite environment. The platform\'s strong preference for Vite and its limitations on file watching are a key factor. I\'m prioritizing building a *conceptually* similar project to a Next.js approach, within the Vite framework to ensure compatibility. The `vite.config.ts` file\'s overrides for the platform, especially `DISABLE_HMR`, solidify the importance of this decision. Switching to Next.js seems problematic, but conceptually I can meet all the user\'s needs.\n\n\n**Implementing Next.js Solution**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Next.js solution. Given the user\'s explicit preference, I\'m setting up the App Router environment. I will follow the standard install for `next` and then build out `app/page.tsx`. I believe this will meet user requirements. The platform\'s file server is already taken care of, so I\'m focusing on the core Next.js setup.\n\n\n**Executing Phase 1**\n\nI\'m now solely focused on Phase 1. I\'m transforming the existing project to Next.js by removing Vite and related dependencies. I will add the Next.js and Supabase dependencies. I need to create the essential Next.js files: `app/layout.tsx` and `app/page.tsx` now. This is a critical step, and then I can pause, as instructed. I need to be sure to update the `package.json` file.\n\n\n**Integrating Supabase**\n\nI\'m now integrating Supabase into the Next.js project, as requested. I\'m focusing on the `lib/supabaseClient.ts` file, configuring the client with `persistSession: false, autoRefreshToken: false, detectSessionInUrl: false`. I\'m setting up `.env.local.example` and adding `.env.local` to `.gitignore`. I will then ensure the project runs before building the UI.\n\n\n**Defining Implementation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the file structure and installation process for Next.js and Supabase integration. I\'ll create `app/layout.tsx` and `app/page.tsx`, and will focus on the creation of `.env.local.example`, and the update of `.gitignore`. I also see the need for `lib/supabaseClient.ts`. It seems critical to update `tsconfig.json` and `package.json` for Next.js. I now see the build is run using `npm run build`, and this will run `next build`.\n\n\n**Refining Configuration**\n\nI\'m now refining the Next.js setup. I realized potential build failures might arise from TypeScript errors, but I don\'t think I need `eslint-config-next`, as I have already confirmed the required types are there. I\'ve moved `src/index.css` to `app/globals.css` for global styling. I\'ve updated the `package.json` scripts to reflect the Next.js environment, and to run on port 3000. Finally, I\'m constructing `app/layout.tsx`.\n\n\n\n**Validating the Environment**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `app/page.tsx`, `app/globals.css`, and `lib/supabaseClient.ts` files, as specified. However, I\'ve realized that the `!` assertion in `supabaseClient.ts` could cause problems during the build process if the environment variables aren\'t set, as `createClient` would throw. I\'m adding a check to prevent this.\n\n\n**Preventing Build Failures**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `app/page.tsx`, `app/globals.css`, and `lib/supabaseClient.ts` files. However, I\'ve realized the `!` assertion in `supabaseClient.ts` would cause problems during the build process if environment variables aren\'t set. I\'m adding a check to prevent build failures. I\'m also updating `.env.local.example` and `.gitignore` as needed. I\'m making progress on the integration!\n\n\n**Finalizing Core Files**\n\nI\'m now generating core files as planned, having successfully integrated Next.js and Supabase. Specifically, I\'m working on `app/layout.tsx` and `app/page.tsx` now. I have edited `package.json`, and configured the essential environment variables, and the `tsconfig.json`. I have also made several updates to ensure that the project runs smoothly, and is ready for further implementation.\n\n\n"
