  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed **Phase 1** of the College Hub Launcher build. \n\nHere is what was accomplished:\n- **Converted to Next.js**: Replaced the default Vite environment with a fully configured Next.js (App Router, TypeScript) project.\n- **Supabase Integration**: Installed `@supabase/supabase-js` and created `/lib/supabaseClient.ts`. The client is strictly configured with `persistSession: false`, `autoRefreshToken: false`, and `detectSessionInUrl: false` to ensure no persistent sessions across tabs or reloads.\n- **Environment Setup**: Created `.env.local.example` listing the required variables and added `.env.local` to `.gitignore`. No keys are hardcoded in the source code.\n- **Validation**: Verified that the Next.js project builds correctly and the local development server starts without any errors.\n\n### What you need to do before we continue:\n\n1. Go to your **Supabase Project Dashboard**.\n2. Navigate to **Project Settings** (the gear icon on the left sidebar) > **API**.\n3. Under the **Project URL** section, copy your URL.\n4. Under the **Project API keys** section, copy the `anon` / `public` key.\n5. Open the `.env.local` file (or the Secrets panel if you\'re running this in a hosted environment) and fill in the following variables:\n   ```env\n   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=\"<your-project-url>\"\n   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=\"<your-anon-key>\"\n   ```\n\n**Definition of Done Checklist (Phase 1):**\n- [x] Project builds and runs locally with no errors.\n- [x] Supabase client initializes with no console errors when env vars are filled in.\n- [x] `.env.local.example` exists and lists both required variables.\n- [x] `.env.local` is in `.gitignore` and not committed.\n- [x] No Supabase URL or key appears hardcoded anywhere in the source.\n\nPlease configure the environment variables on your end and let me know when you are ready to proceed to **Phase 2 (Login page)**!"
    thinking: "**Finalizing Phase 1**\n\nOkay, I\'m now composing the concluding summary for Phase 1. I\'m double-checking the checklist to ensure everything is accounted for before stopping tool calls to await further instructions.\n\n\n**Establishing Supabase Connection**\n\nI\'ve crafted `lib/supabaseClient.ts` to connect, prioritizing security with disabled session persistence, auto-refresh, and URL detection. I\'ve added `.env.local.example` and updated `.gitignore`, and have confirmed the project\'s ability to run. Now, I\'m documenting clear instructions for obtaining and inputting the Supabase credentials, so the user knows what env vars to fill in and where to get them from their Supabase project dashboard.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed **Phase 1** of the College Hub Launcher build. \n\nHere is what was accomplished:\n- **Converted to Next.js**: Replaced the default Vite environment with a fully configured Next.js (App Router, TypeScript) project.\n- **Supabase Integration**: Installed `@supabase/supabase-js` and created `/lib/supabaseClient.ts`. The client is strictly configured with `persistSession: false`, `autoRefreshToken: false`, and `detectSessionInUrl: false` to ensure no persistent sessions across tabs or reloads.\n- **Environment Setup**: Created `.env.local.example` listing the required variables and added `.env.local` to `.gitignore`. No keys are hardcoded in the source code.\n- **Validation**: Verified that the Next.js project builds correctly and the local development server starts without any errors.\n\n### What you need to do before we continue:\n\n1. Go to your **Supabase Project Dashboard**.\n2. Navigate to **Project Settings** (the gear icon on the left sidebar) > **API**.\n3. Under the **Project URL** section, copy your URL.\n4. Under the **Project API keys** section, copy the `anon` / `public` key.\n5. Open the `.env.local` file (or the Secrets panel if you\'re running this in a hosted environment) and fill in the following variables:\n   ```env\n   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=\"<your-project-url>\"\n   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=\"<your-anon-key>\"\n   ```\n\n**Definition of Done Checklist (Phase 1):**\n- [x] Project builds and runs locally with no errors.\n- [x] Supabase client initializes with no console errors when env vars are filled in.\n- [x] `.env.local.example` exists and lists both required variables.\n- [x] `.env.local` is in `.gitignore` and not committed.\n- [x] No Supabase URL or key appears hardcoded anywhere in the source.\n\nPlease configure the environment variables on your end and let me know when you are ready to proceed to **Phase 2 (Login page)**!"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 444463530
    }
