n\nI\'ve decided to prioritize Phase 2, directly integrating the \"Bento Grid\" theme. I\'m focusing on \"building\" the Login Page based on the user\'s explicit command. My next steps involve reviewing Phase 2 requirements, starting with the Login Page implementation at `app/page.tsx`, and integrating Supabase authentication within a try/catch block for error handling. I\'ll need to show a loading state on the button during sign-in.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Login**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the login page. I\'ve included a redirect to `/dashboard` on successful authentication and error messaging from Supabase on failure. I\'m skipping the signup form for now, and I\'ll now be writing the full code for `/app/page.tsx`, implementing the `use client` directive, necessary imports, and the login form logic using React hooks. I\'ve verified the `@` import alias for the Supabase client.\n\n\n**Constructing the Login Page**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the front-end login form, using `useRouter`, `useState`, and form handling. I\'ve integrated email and password state, with loading and error handling. I\'m building a function to call Supabase auth, displaying errors, and redirecting on success. The form includes validation and a loading state. I\'m using a try/catch for auth errors, and I am planning to implement the layout styling.\n\n\n**Styling the Login Form**\n\nI\'m now incorporating styling for the login form, focusing on a black border with rounded corners, padding, and a shadow effect. I\'m building out a container with a black border, rounded corners, padding, a flex column layout and a shadow. Inside, I\'m working on the college logo and the introductory text. I\'ll need to handle the state and validation inside the form, including the error messaging.\n\n\n**Refining the Input Fields**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the email and password input fields within the login form. I\'m adding a black border with rounded corners, padding, and a transition effect. I\'ve included placeholder text, and am building in custom styling, like `bg-slate-50` and focus states for visual feedback. These are critical for the login page\'s user experience.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Login Button**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the login button, refining its visual state changes. I\'m focusing on disabled, loading, and active styles to make it a better experience. I\'m applying the required styles for this element.\n\n\n**Integrating the Bento Theme**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Bento Grid theme, but I\'ll maintain the Phase 2 requirements. I\'m updating `app/layout.tsx` to match the background color and font constraints. I\'m also preparing to edit both `app/globals.css` and `app/page.tsx`, and will pause to confirm it works. I\'m moving toward the light background, neon yellow, hard shadows and border-2 black Bento Grid style.\n\n\n"
