  planner_response {
    response: "I\'ve resolved the issue with the development server. \n\n### What went wrong:\nThe issue was caused by conflicting React versions across the project\'s setup (specifically, an incompatibility between the latest Next.js 14 and React 19). \n\n### What I did to fix it:\n1. Traced the issue to a `TypeError` coming from a `next build` failure due to React context mismatches.\n2. Cleaned out `node_modules` and the `package-lock.json` file completely.\n3. Updated the project to use **Next.js 15**, which has native and stable support for React 19 (the version you were already using for other libraries).\n4. Restarted the platform\'s development server.\n\nThe server should now be running the Next.js `dev` script successfully, and the Bento Grid login page should be live in your preview pane. Let me know if it\'s up for you and if you\'re ready for **Phase 3 (Dashboard)**!"
    modified_response: "I\'ve resolved the issue with the development server. \n\n### What went wrong:\nThe issue was caused by conflicting React versions across the project\'s setup (specifically, an incompatibility between the latest Next.js 14 and React 19). \n\n### What I did to fix it:\n1. Traced the issue to a `TypeError` coming from a `next build` failure due to React context mismatches.\n2. Cleaned out `node_modules` and the `package-lock.json` file completely.\n3. Updated the project to use **Next.js 15**, which has native and stable support for React 19 (the version you were already using for other libraries).\n4. Restarted the platform\'s development server.\n\nThe server should now be running the Next.js `dev` script successfully, and the Bento Grid login page should be live in your preview pane. Let me know if it\'s up for you and if you\'re ready for **Phase 3 (Dashboard)**!"
